<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Two Australians dead from contaminated meat.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Two Australians dead from contaminated meat.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two Australians had died in the southern state of Victoria after eating contaminated meats, a spokesman for the state's health department said on Friday.</p>
<p>A spokesman for the Department of Human Services and Health said the deaths, which occurred in the last couple of weeks, had led to the voluntary recall of some ham and silverside products.</p>
<p>He said chief health officer Graham Rouch was preparing a statement and would hold a news conference at 10.30 a.m. (2330 GMT) to release further details about the situation.</p>
<p>No further information was available.</p>
<p>-- Melbourne Bureau 61-3 9286-1421</p>
</text>
